/* Muro, English. The master list: every other language has the same keys.
   A key with @@ carries a context (one English word, two meanings elsewhere).
   A key with # is one form of a counted line: #one, #other, and in some
   languages #few, #many, or #=1 for exactly one. %@ is a value; %1$@ and
   %2$@ name which one, so a language can put them in its own order. */

